| `secrets.scanner.install_root` | string | `~/.cache/<project_slug>/tools`: `~/.cache/my_project/tools` by default, `~/.cache/project_keel/tools` in keel | an absolute path or one under `~/`, with no `..` part, never inside the checkout | `scripts/install_scanner.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `secrets.scanner.install_root` row | Moves the per-user directory `make secrets-install` installs the scanner under, as `<install_root>/<name>/<rev>/<name>` beside the kept release archive, which a second run checks against the pinned sha256 and the program against, byte for byte. A root, or a program path a link under it leads, inside the checkout is exit 14 before any fetch, because git would list the program; a root this user cannot write is exit 2 naming it; outside it, the target changes nothing git lists and stays `[read]`. Required: absent, the installer is exit 14 naming this key. The program and kept archive must resolve inside this authorized root, including through existing parents; an escape or symlink loop is exit 14 before any fetch or mutation. | where the record lives: `secrets.scanner.record_file` | always |
